{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>They</b> — for they did not ask of HaShem to make Jeroboam king, and it is written: \"whom YHWH your Elohim chooses\" (Deuteronomy 17:15) — so too shall the king of Israel be." "<b>They made princes</b> — from the root עלם, the ayin is quiescent. The form שר is duplicated, and the meaning is doubled. And Yefet said: it is like samekh, as in שורי מהם (Hosea 8:4), and the meaning is reversed: whether they made them kings or whether they made them princes. And the meaning of למען יכרת — \"in order that it be cut off from them\" — is the silver and the gold."], :book :hosea, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :notes {1 "The phrase והטעם כפול likely refers to the doubled form שרשר or similar understood duplicate; left literal as Ibn Ezra's compressed syntax is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Hosea -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=15&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:50:37.229146475Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}